  "goodToKnow": "Der Kamerad (die Kameradin) is a comrade, especially in the army or fire brigade, or a mate: der Schulkamerad, der Spielkamerad. It's a weak noun: den Kameraden. A political comrade, in socialist parties, is der Genosse instead. Die Kameradschaft is camaraderie. Because of its use in Nazi-era and far-right groups, Kamerad can carry overtones there, so context matters. From French camarade, roommate."
